@startuml
!theme plain
title Model Readiness and Evaluation Data Flow
rectangle "Candidate Data Sources" as SOURCES
rectangle "Rights, Privacy & Provenance Gate" as GATE
rectangle "Quarantine" as QUAR
rectangle "Curation & De-identification" as CURATE
rectangle "Dataset Registry & Manifests" as REG
rectangle "Runtime Retrieval Corpus" as RAG
rectangle "Prompt/Workflow Exemplars" as PROMPT
rectangle "Held-out Evaluation Sets" as EVAL
rectangle "Red-team & Safety Sets" as RED
rectangle "Future Fine-tuning Candidate" as FT
rectangle "Model/Prompt Release Candidate" as MODEL
rectangle "Automated Evaluation" as AUTO
rectangle "Human Academic Review" as HUMAN
rectangle "Security, Privacy & Tenant Tests" as SEC
rectangle "Release Gate" as RELEASE
rectangle "Approved Release" as PROD

SOURCES --> GATE
GATE --> QUAR : unclear rights / sensitive / incomplete
GATE --> CURATE : admissible
CURATE --> REG
REG --> RAG : runtime context permitted
REG --> PROMPT : exemplar use permitted
REG --> EVAL : evaluation-only split
REG --> RED : safety-only split
REG --> FT : only after explicit model-use approval
PROMPT --> MODEL
RAG --> MODEL
MODEL --> AUTO
EVAL --> AUTO
MODEL --> HUMAN
EVAL --> HUMAN
MODEL --> SEC
RED --> SEC
AUTO --> RELEASE
HUMAN --> RELEASE
SEC --> RELEASE
RELEASE --> MODEL : fail → remediate
RELEASE --> PROD : pass + documented approval

note bottom of EVAL
Held-out evaluation cases are excluded from training
and contamination-checked before each release.
end note
@enduml
